<speak><prosody pitch="1.17st" rate="1.03">Here are three healthy dinner ideas: **Option 1: Grilled Chicken and Roasted Vegetables** * Grill chicken breast with olive oil, salt, and pepper * Roast a variety of colorful vegetables like broccoli, carrots, bell peppers, and Brussels sprouts with olive oil, salt, and pepper * Serve with quinoa or brown rice and a drizzle of balsamic glaze **Option 2: Baked Salmon and Sweet Potato** * Season salmon fillets with lemon juice, garlic powder, and paprika * Bake in the oven with sliced sweet potatoes (drizzled with olive oil and salt) for 12-15 minutes or until cooked through * Serve with steamed green beans or a side salad **Option 3: Lentil and Vegetable Stew** * Saute onions, garlic, and carrots in olive oil * Add lentils, diced tomatoes, vegetable broth, and your favorite spices (e.</prosody><break time="520ms"/><break time="120ms"/><prosody pitch="0.24st" rate="1.02">g.</prosody><break time="520ms"/><prosody pitch="0.61st" rate="1.02">, cumin, paprika) * Simmer for 20-25 minutes or until the lentils are tender * Serve with whole grain bread or a side of steamed asparagus These dinner ideas are not only delicious but also packed with nutrients, fiber, and protein to keep you full and satisfied!</prosody><break time="520ms"/><break time="120ms"/></speak>